Surfaced during karr #11 (CLI/Cmd/Item.pm never sent includeComponents=true, invisible offline). t/lib/MockUA.pm serves the same fixture file regardless of query string, so any bug where the code fails to pass a required query param (includeComponents, includeLoot, etc.) cannot be caught by the offline suite -- only live testing (or a live-API opt-in run) surfaces it.

Idea (not committed to, needs design): teach MockUA to notice includeComponents/includeLoot presence and strip the gated fields from the response when absent, so a missing query param produces a visibly different (leaner) fixture response and existing assertions on those fields would fail offline. Would need care not to churn every existing fixture/test. Low priority -- this is a testing-infra improvement, not a live bug.

MockUA strippt components/recycle_components/sold_by (/items ohne includeComponents=true) und loot (/arcs ohne includeLoot=true); Fixtures unverändert. t/33-mockua-query-gating.t neu; Gegenprobe: ohne includeComponents in CLI/Cmd/Item.pm wird t/30-cli.t rot (10 Fehlschläge), danach zurückgesetzt. prove -lr t: 19 Dateien, PASS. Offen: Live-Verhalten ohne Flag nicht verifiziert (offline) – leere Arrays angenommen; von Getty zu bestätigen.
